    {
      "id": 1,
      "sentence": "Why do you think the way you do?",
      "paragraph_id": 0,
      "word_count": 8,
      "start_time": 3.05,
      "end_time": 5.475,
      "duration": 2.425,
      "phoneme_count": 31
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "sentence": "What do you think might be the best way for scientists to try to prove if life exists beyond Earth?",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 20,
      "start_time": 5.475,
      "end_time": 12.275,
      "duration": 6.8,
      "phoneme_count": 101
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "sentence": "Read the New York Times article \u201cLurking Inside an Asteroid: Life\u2019s Ingredients,\u201d published on Jan. 29.",
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "word_count": 16,
      "start_time": 12.275,
      "end_time": 20.725,
      "duration": 8.45,
      "phoneme_count": 116
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "sentence": "It begins:",
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "word_count": 2,
      "start_time": 20.725,
      "end_time": 22.425,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "phoneme_count": 12
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "sentence": "Our solar system contains planets, dwarf planets, asteroids and comets \u2014 but only one world is known to harbor life.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 20,
      "start_time": 22.425,
      "end_time": 31.45,
      "duration": 9.025,
      "phoneme_count": 128
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "sentence": "Scientists have long debated whether Earth is truly unique.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 9,
      "start_time": 31.45,
      "end_time": 35.675,
      "duration": 4.225,
      "phoneme_count": 59
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "sentence": "Perhaps our planet just happened to have the right combination of ingredients, conditions and timing to allow life to emerge.",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 20,
      "start_time": 35.675,
      "end_time": 44.275,
      "duration": 8.6,
      "phoneme_count": 126
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "sentence": "But a pinch of grit from a distant asteroid collected by a NASA spacecraft holds hints that our planet may not be so special.",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 24,
      "start_time": 44.275,
      "end_time": 53.0,
      "duration": 8.725,
      "phoneme_count": 136
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "sentence": "A team of researchers reported in the journal Nature on Wednesday that the asteroid, known as Bennu, contains a wealth of organic molecules, including many crucial building blocks of life.",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 30,
      "start_time": 53.0,
      "end_time": 65.975,
      "duration": 12.975,
      "phoneme_count": 187
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "sentence": "The chemistry that produced them might be going on today on the ice moons of Jupiter and Saturn.",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 18,
      "start_time": 65.975,
      "end_time": 72.775,
      "duration": 6.8,
      "phoneme_count": 96
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "sentence": "\u201cOur odds of finding life elsewhere are increasing,\u201d said Daniel Glavin, a senior scientist for sample return at NASA\u2019s Goddard Space Flight Center and a co-author of the two papers.",
